5. Functional Requirements
FR1 – User Authentication
The system should allow users to:
•	Register an account.
•	Log in.
•	Log out.
•	Reset/change their password.
•	Manage basic profile information.
Authentication can also be implemented using an external identity provider if desired.
FR2 – Create Comic Project
Users should be able to create a new project by entering:
•	Comic title
•	Story idea
•	Genre
•	Target audience
•	Number of pages/panels
•	Art style
•	Language
•	Optional character information
Example:
Title: The Last Robot
Genre: Science Fiction
Idea: A robot discovers that it is the last intelligent machine on Earth.
________________________________________
FR3 – AI Story Generation
The system should send the user's prompt and relevant project information to a Gemini model.
Gemini should generate:
•	Story title
•	Story summary
•	Beginning
•	Conflict
•	Climax
•	Resolution
•	Characters
•	Scene descriptions
The generated result should be displayed to the user for editing.
________________________________________
FR4 – Character Generation
ComicCraft should allow users to create characters manually or with AI.
For each character, the system can store:
•	Character name
•	Age/category
•	Personality
•	Appearance
•	Role
•	Background
•	Abilities
•	Relationships with other characters
Example:
Name: Alex
Role: Protagonist
Personality: Curious and brave
Appearance: Black hair, blue jacket
________________________________________
FR5 – Comic Panel Generation
The generated story should be divided into panels.
Each panel may contain:
•	Panel number
•	Scene description
•	Characters present
•	Character actions
•	Background
•	Dialogue
•	Narration
•	Image-generation prompt
Example:
Panel 1
Scene: A ruined city at sunset.

Characters:
Alex

Action:
Alex walks through the abandoned street.

Narration:
"The city had been silent for twenty years."

Dialogue:
Alex: "Is anyone still here?"
________________________________________
FR6 – Dialogue Generation
Gemini should generate dialogue appropriate to:
•	Character personality
•	Scene context
•	Story genre
•	Emotional situation
Users should be able to manually modify generated dialogue.
________________________________________
FR7 – Image Generation / Visual Prompt Generation
The system should create visual descriptions for each comic panel.
Depending on the selected implementation, the application can:
•	Generate prompts for an image-generation model.
•	Generate images through a compatible image-generation service/model.
•	Allow users to upload their own images.
The system should attempt to maintain visual consistency between panels, especially for recurring characters.
________________________________________
FR8 – Comic Editor
Users should be able to edit:
•	Story
•	Characters
•	Panels
•	Dialogue
•	Narration
•	Images
•	Panel order
Basic operations should include:
•	Add panel
•	Delete panel
•	Duplicate panel
•	Reorder panels
•	Edit text
•	Replace image
________________________________________
FR9 – Comic Preview
The system should provide a preview mode showing the comic approximately as it will appear after export.
Users should be able to navigate between:
•	Pages
•	Panels
•	Characters
•	Scenes
________________________________________
FR10 – Save Project
Users should be able to save their projects.
A project should contain:
Project
 ├── Metadata
 ├── Story
 ├── Characters
 ├── Scenes
 ├── Panels
 ├── Images
 └── Export settings
________________________________________
FR11 – Export Comic
The application should allow users to export the finished comic.
Possible formats:
•	PDF
•	PNG/JPEG pages
•	Digital comic format
For the initial version, PDF and image export are sufficient.
________________________________________
FR12 – Project Management
Users should be able to:
•	View previous projects
•	Open a project
•	Rename a project
•	Duplicate a project
•	Delete a project
•	Continue editing an unfinished project
________________________________________
6. Non-Functional Requirements
Performance
•	AI requests should provide feedback while processing.
•	The UI should remain responsive during AI generation.
•	Large projects should load efficiently.
Security
•	User authentication must be secure.
•	API keys must never be exposed in frontend code.
•	User project data should be protected.
•	Access to projects should be restricted to authorized users.
Scalability
The architecture should allow additional AI models and image-generation services to be added later.
Usability
The interface should be:
•	Simple
•	Beginner-friendly
•	Responsive
•	Easy to navigate
•	Suitable for desktop and tablet devices
Reliability
The system should handle:
•	AI generation failures
•	Network failures
•	Invalid prompts
•	API rate limits
•	Incomplete AI responses
Graceful error messages should be provided to users.
